#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Lexicon lifecycle\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lexicons are designed to be machine-readable and network-accessible. While it is not currently *required* that a Lexicon is available on the network, it is strongly advised to publish Lexicons so that a single canonical & authoritative representation is available to consumers of the method.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lexicons are published to a PDS like any other AT record. They are resolved using DNS TXT records to link [NSID namespaces](/specs/nsid) to PDS repositories, so that when you address a Lexicon like `com.atproto.example,` atproto SDKs will know to [look for an identity at `atproto.com`](https://pds.ls/at://did:plc:6msi3pj7krzih5qxqtryxlzw/com.atproto.lexicon.schema) and retrieve the Lexicon from there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "For an NSID like `app.toy.record`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- The final segment `record` is the record/method name\n"
"- The authority is `app.toy`; reversed, this becomes the domain `toy.app`\n"
"- The DNS TXT record goes at `_lexicon.toy.app`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each unique namespace prefix requires its own DNS TXT record, pointing to your DID. For example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"_lexicon.toy.app      TXT \"did=did:plc:abc123...\"\n"
"_lexicon.like.toy.app TXT \"did=did:plc:abc123...\"\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Using goat\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use [`goat`](https://github.com/bluesky-social/goat), our command line tool, for creating and publishing Lexicons. The Lexicon-related features are available under [`goat lex`](https://github.com/bluesky-social/goat?tab=readme-ov-file#lexicon-development) :\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- publishing schemas to and synchronizing from the AT network\n"
"- diffing, linting, and verifying schema evolution rules\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "`goat` can be installed from [Homebrew](https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/goat) on macOS and Linux:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "<BrewInstallGoat />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a project directory, you can download some existing Lexicons, which will get saved as JSON files in `./lexicons/`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "<GoatLexPull />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also create a new Lexicon record with `goat lex new record`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "<GoatLexNew />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "And eventually publish it with `goat lex publish`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "<GoatLexPublish />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/publishing-lexicons/en.mdx:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Note>\n"
"You'll need to log in with `goat` to publish to your PDS! To do this, use `goat account login` or set the `GOAT_USERNAME` and `GOAT_PASSWORD` environment variables.\n"
"</Note>\n"
msgstr ""

